<pipeline>
  <info>
    <name>trf_data_vault_multiactive_sat_generic_source_is_STG</name>
    <name_sync_with_filename>Y</name_sync_with_filename>
    <description>Generic transformation: multiactive_hub satellite</description>
    <extended_description>This transformation loads a multiactive Data Vault hub-satellite.
To determine whether one of the attributes has changed a concatenated string including all source attributes separated by a |
is compared to the equivalent concatenation in de Data Vault.

The 'sat_multiactive_extra_key_column' specifies the column that causes the satellite to have a different cardinality than the hub.
Example: if a satellite contains the phone numbers of an employee, the type of phone number (e.g. home, work) could be used to
have a multiactive satellite with one active entry per phone number type.
There can be only be one such column in a hub satellite, although you could make it an concatenated one.
</extended_description>
    <pipeline_version>1.10</pipeline_version>
    <pipeline_type>Normal</pipeline_type>
    <pipeline_status>2</pipeline_status>
    <directory>/data_vault</directory>
